  "id": "Compound::DB00988 - Gene::6582",
  "verbalization": "Dopamine is shown to interact with Slc22a3 through binding, which is then linked to a transporter activity that is participated by Slc22a2. This suggests a potential role for Slc22a2 in dopamine transport, as it is involved in the activity of Slc22a3, which is itself a transporter for dopamine. Similarly, Dopamine binds to Slc22a1, which in turn participates in dopamine transport, and this pathway also leads to Slc22a2. The evidence suggests that Slc22a2 may be a downstream component in the dopamine transport pathway, possibly involved in the transmembrane movement of dopamine. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which dopamine interacts with Slc22a2, though the exact functional role remains to be determined.",
